6 Larch Grove is not in a conservation area. Our records also show it is not a listed building and has no tree preservation order.

Because it isn't in a conservation area, replacing the windows is unlikely to need planning permission just for being in one. The council guidance says that replacement windows in a conservation area need an application unless they match the existing windows in material and pattern. That rule doesn't apply to your property.

I can't give a formal planning opinion, so if you're unsure whether your specific works are [withheld] development, check with the planning desk before you start. If you have any existing planning application reference for the property, I can look up its details too.
